 That's what they're saying.

02:17:39.940 --> 02:17:40.480
 It's...

02:17:40.480 --> 02:17:41.120
 They said...

02:17:41.120 --> 02:17:43.840
 Yes, Silver Lake and 40% of Brookhaven.

02:17:44.840 --> 02:17:45.840
 But it'll split...

02:17:45.840 --> 02:17:47.300
 It'll split to bring more of the...

02:17:47.300 --> 02:17:48.720
 It'll bring more.

02:17:48.720 --> 02:17:51.000
 Yeah, it'll bring further west.

02:17:51.660 --> 02:17:53.160
 Yeah, because I thought this was supposed to be healthy.

02:17:53.160 --> 02:17:54.640
 It's going to bring some Cedar Bollies.

02:17:54.760 --> 02:17:55.160
 All right.

02:17:55.300 --> 02:17:55.780
 All right.

02:17:55.780 --> 02:17:56.000
 All right.

02:17:56.000 --> 02:17:56.660
 All right.

02:17:57.660 --> 02:18:03.720
 Either way, I'm just saying we would be fooling ourselves if we didn't...

02:18:03.720 --> 02:18:06.560
 There will be some impact through those neighborhoods.

02:18:06.560 --> 02:18:06.960
 There's going to be...

02:18:06.960 --> 02:18:07.140
 Yeah.

02:18:07.240 --> 02:18:07.500
 Yeah.

02:18:07.740 --> 02:18:13.820
 And I think, you know, if you built the high school in the north end, you're going to have

02:18:13.820 --> 02:18:16.840
 some impact just in different neighborhoods.

02:18:17.060 --> 02:18:20.900
 People do tend to drive the path of least resistance.

02:18:21.460 --> 02:18:26.400
 Well, I'll tell you, the areas that we talked about, just so you know, there were three areas

02:18:26.400 --> 02:18:27.160
 that we talked about.

02:18:27.300 --> 02:18:30.960
 There's the mine that Julie brought up.

02:18:31.460 --> 02:18:38.360
 Chris and I and Jared talked about the possibility of engaging with Wadsworth with the south, excuse

02:18:38.360 --> 02:18:45.420
 me, the northwest corner of Mountain View Corridor and SR-73, and maybe even the possibility

02:18:45.420 --> 02:18:53.140
 of back in the canyon to the west of Wildflower, which would have access points on major roads

02:18:53.140 --> 02:18:56.480
 to get back in there that you would be impacting neighborhoods with.

02:18:56.860 --> 02:19:02.040
 And I think we definitely need to keep all of those locations in mind because as soon as

02:19:02.040 --> 02:19:07.360
 we get one high school started, we'll go back to 80 and we start on a second.

02:19:07.540 --> 02:19:09.580
 I think this high school...

02:19:09.580 --> 02:19:11.440
 I think it's got to be closer to Cedar Valley.

02:19:11.580 --> 02:19:13.280
 I don't think it's got to be closer to Firefly.

02:19:13.700 --> 02:19:14.140
 Yeah.

02:19:14.760 --> 02:19:15.820
 That's the next impact.

02:19:16.900 --> 02:19:23.400
 But also remember, I mean, I just attended a meeting at a junior high last night with

02:19:23.400 --> 02:19:26.440
 another 1,200 homes coming in.

02:19:27.060 --> 02:19:28.200
 That's 2,100.

02:19:29.200 --> 02:19:30.860
 That's your run-up against the mountain there.

02:19:31.220 --> 02:19:31.900
 The simple property.

02:19:32.000 --> 02:19:33.420
 I mean, you're going to help.

02:19:33.740 --> 02:19:34.340
 I mean, everywhere.

02:19:35.880 --> 02:19:37.000
 Everybody keeps saying that's happening.

02:19:37.100 --> 02:19:37.660
 It's not happening.

02:19:38.540 --> 02:19:39.300
 It's not happening yet.

02:19:39.700 --> 02:19:41.700
 Chris is like over my dead body.

02:19:42.320 --> 02:19:44.100
 I was in the main area.

02:19:44.100 --> 02:19:46.180
 Yeah, it hasn't been approved.

02:19:46.180 --> 02:19:47.160
 It's not happening.

02:19:47.160 --> 02:19:47.560
 It hasn't been approved.

02:19:47.560 --> 02:19:47.680
 Yeah.

02:19:48.680 --> 02:19:49.680
 That's a negotiation.

02:19:50.060 --> 02:19:53.560
 But they'll be breaking ground in the spring for land that's not annexed.

02:19:55.280 --> 02:19:56.880
 You're such a troublemaker today.

02:19:56.880 --> 02:19:58.960
 You're a little bit contentious today.

02:20:00.600 --> 02:20:02.700
 Chris ate all my M&M's, you guys.

02:20:03.640 --> 02:20:04.980
 He hasn't gotten to his $50.

02:20:05.520 --> 02:20:10.620
 You were a little late.

02:20:10.740 --> 02:20:11.400
 It was pretty good.

02:20:11.940 --> 02:20:13.620
 Does this site alleviate...

02:20:13.620 --> 02:20:14.720
 Does this site alleviate...

02:20:14.720 --> 02:20:16.400
 There's no question.

02:20:16.400 --> 02:20:19.060
 Like Rich said, it's the least of the worst.

02:20:19.560 --> 02:20:20.020
 You know what I mean?

02:20:20.580 --> 02:20:23.840
 But we need a school...

02:20:23.840 --> 02:20:24.700
 And Julie's right.

02:20:25.700 --> 02:20:30.140
 The problem is aggravated by the number of kids that have to go to these schools.

02:20:30.660 --> 02:20:36.240
 Because when you put almost double the amount of kids in a school, it just brings more traffic to it.

02:20:36.400 --> 02:20:40.740
 Traffic studies are done for the number of people that the school is built for.

02:20:41.040 --> 02:20:47.920
 Hey, Julie, and maybe, Julie, you know, is this school being built for the typical 1,700 to 2,200 capacity?

02:20:48.540 --> 02:20:49.920
 It is being built.

02:20:50.120 --> 02:20:52.960
 Like the square footage is going to be roughly the same.

02:20:54.260 --> 02:21:03.360
 The goal is that at opening, roughly every high school, Westlake, Cedar Valley, and the new would be around 2,100 kids.

02:21:04.220 --> 02:21:04.360
 Okay.

02:21:05.060 --> 02:21:09.560
 Yeah, an actual cafeteria, that'd be nice.

02:21:09.560 --> 02:21:11.240
 I will say it's also fascinating.

02:21:11.400 --> 02:21:19.040
 I'm down in Washington County right now, and I went and toured two of their high schools because they've been doing some interesting stuff with construction just to get some ideas from them.

02:21:19.500 --> 02:21:22.780
 Their typical high school, what they build for, is 1,500.

02:21:23.580 --> 02:21:31.480
 So part of it is it's hard to do comparables when other areas are not building schools to house the number of kids we are.

02:21:32.060 --> 02:21:32.500
 Yeah.

02:21:33.740 --> 02:21:37.040
 And that absolutely impacts the traffic flow.

02:21:37.380 --> 02:21:40.440
 And, Rich, I'm sorry that I'm, like, biting your head off about this.

02:21:41.080 --> 02:21:42.080
 Oh, I can handle it.

02:21:42.240 --> 02:21:42.700
 By the way.

02:21:43.020 --> 02:21:46.420
 I don't have a problem about, you know, conversations.

02:21:46.420 --> 02:21:48.580
 I mean, we've talked about the traffic issues.

02:21:48.580 --> 02:21:56.680
 We've talked about it, but at the same time, we've never held, like, an official meeting or to the point where you guys have said, hey, we've engaged the landowner.

02:21:56.760 --> 02:21:57.680
 So I don't have a problem.

02:21:58.000 --> 02:22:12.880
 And I think for the next high school, like, one of the first things I want to do is sit down and have a very long, like, two-hour come-to-Jesus conversation about where do you guys, based on the development of the city, where do you guys think that we need to buy land for high schools and middles?

02:22:12.880 --> 02:22:25.520
 We did originally buy the property where the middle school is going for a high school and a middle, but we don't have enough acreage right now with the gulch running through it to make that feasible.

02:22:25.520 --> 02:22:30.220
 So we can probably do an elementary, but not a high school like we had intended.

02:22:30.720 --> 02:22:37.120
 So now we've got to look at other options for where we're going to place the next Eagle Mountain Middle or the ex-Eagle Mountain High School.

02:22:37.140 --> 02:22:40.060
 And I think that definitely is something we need to have a conversation about.

02:22:40.300 --> 02:22:41.940
 It's just hard at this point.

02:22:41.980 --> 02:22:42.860
 Like, I get it.

02:22:42.880 --> 02:22:47.120
 It's not a done deal 100%, but we've invested millions in the architecture.

02:22:47.120 --> 02:22:59.120
 For me to go back to the board and say, we want to screw it over, I mean, people are already, like, it's going to be a hard enough of an ask to try and get the lease revenue bond done.

02:22:59.580 --> 02:23:01.540
 We're millions in architecture?

02:23:02.060 --> 02:23:03.820
 Yeah, we've set aside about 8 million.

02:23:04.480 --> 02:23:10.680
 It's generally a percentage of what the build is going to cost, and we're about 8 million in, I believe.

02:23:11.120 --> 02:23:17.640
 And this isn't a complaint about board members.

02:23:17.820 --> 02:23:21.840
 This is a complaint about the process.

02:23:22.320 --> 02:23:25.640
 And I'm not taking it as, like, a personal attack at all.

02:23:25.780 --> 02:23:30.380
 I just, we've had so many problems with this site, which I know you guys are right.

02:23:30.460 --> 02:23:34.820
 Like, some people, right, some board members are saying we're good to go, everything's fine and peachy keen.

02:23:35.120 --> 02:23:41.000
 And everything, I feel like, on our side, at least where Joy Lynn and I sit, has been a fight.

02:23:41.180 --> 02:23:45.940
 And I think it's still going to be a fight to get the funding, even if we get the legislation through.

02:23:46.240 --> 02:23:48.960
 They may choose not to fund this high school out of spite.

02:23:50.180 --> 02:23:51.020
 I just...

02:23:51.020 --> 02:23:52.720
 We appreciate that, Julian.

02:23:52.880 --> 02:23:58.960
 The reality is the reason that we haven't been having this fight is because there was a bigger fight to have first.

02:23:59.260 --> 02:23:59.540
 Right.

02:23:59.700 --> 02:24:04.740
 And I think we haven't been engaged in that same fight, but it doesn't mean that this isn't one that needs to be discussed.

02:24:04.740 --> 02:24:15.260
 Because at the end of all of this, how it impacts the community that it's in, the students that are going to, that has to always be part of the conversation up front.

02:24:15.500 --> 02:24:15.940
 Right.

02:24:15.940 --> 02:24:18.780
 Not just after the, oh, man, I wish we would have done this differently.

02:24:19.060 --> 02:24:26.640
 Because we have a lot of those in Eagle Mountain and Saratoga Springs, where we're saying, man, I wish we would have done this differently.

02:24:27.100 --> 02:24:29.280
 Or why in the world did we do this?

02:24:29.360 --> 02:24:35.680
 This has such a negative impact on traffic or safety for the kids going to and from.

02:24:36.440 --> 02:24:39.900
 Because initially we thought, you know, it's going to be a bus school.

02:24:40.520 --> 02:24:41.600
 Well, then the buses are gone.

02:24:41.660 --> 02:24:47.940
 And that created a very different environment that didn't exist initially because we didn't think about all the possibilities of that.

02:24:48.520 --> 02:24:51.680
 I just, I love that you're saying, let's sit down and have a two-hour conversation.

02:24:51.680 --> 02:24:53.840
 I think moving forward, no question.

02:24:54.000 --> 02:25:05.640
 I think that's the best way to do things between the school district and the cities so that we're trying to, right, before we've done those things and we can help you with some of those decisions and show, you know,

02:25:05.700 --> 02:25:13.700
 this is the future plan of how this road is going to be so that we don't put schools on a road that's going to be a major collector arterial road.

02:25:13.940 --> 02:25:16.660
 Well, and we can do NDAs if needed, too.

02:25:16.800 --> 02:25:19.840
 Like, if it's, because we do that all the time with RDA type stuff.

02:25:21.200 --> 02:25:28.160
 There's a big difference between us talking to the board and talking to the staff with current Alpine School District.

02:25:28.600 --> 02:25:28.840
 True.

02:25:29.280 --> 02:25:34.960
 Because we do sit down once or twice a year with senior staff at Alpine and the board.

02:25:34.960 --> 02:25:38.700
 And we go through all of our growth projection plans and where all the growth is coming.

02:25:39.220 --> 02:25:43.160
 And then they buy a junior high site on Redwood Road with a canal running right in the middle of it.

02:25:43.900 --> 02:25:45.180
 That site makes no sense.

02:25:47.060 --> 02:25:55.540
 Well, I think there has to be a change that we make on, you know, from Joy Lynn and I's perspective when we've got a new board and new staff coming in.

02:25:55.540 --> 02:25:59.840
 And I think doing some of this work ahead of time, like, I would say we've got a year.

02:25:59.920 --> 02:26:04.140
 We've got a year between, you know, the election and a new board coming in.

02:26:04.400 --> 02:26:05.920
 Let's use that year well.

02:26:06.040 --> 02:26:16.600
 And I think that we should sit down and schedule a conversation and say, okay, looking at your guys' master plan for the city over the next 40 years, where are the sites?

02:26:16.820 --> 02:26:19.160
 What connections do you have with developers?

02:26:19.580 --> 02:26:20.780
 Let's start the conversations.

02:26:20.780 --> 02:26:23.840
 Because we all know that it's not just this school, right?

02:26:23.860 --> 02:26:26.240
 We've got to do an elementary to offset Desert Sky.

02:26:26.520 --> 02:26:28.940
 We've got another high school we've got to figure out.

02:26:29.240 --> 02:26:31.360
 So let's sit down and figure some of that out.

02:26:31.580 --> 02:26:37.140
 Obviously, the new board's going to have to make a call about where they purchase property and who they hire.

02:26:37.700 --> 02:26:39.800
 But let's do some of the legwork now.

02:26:39.980 --> 02:26:42.160
 And I would say we need to do the same thing with Saratoga.

02:26:42.440 --> 02:26:44.100
 Like, let's figure out.

02:26:44.480 --> 02:26:47.360
 I don't think we can solve this issue and this school.

02:26:47.660 --> 02:26:49.700
 I just, that's my perspective.

02:26:50.060 --> 02:26:51.640
 I'm willing to be proven wrong.

02:26:52.320 --> 02:26:59.620
 I feel like we've tried to offset the traffic as much as we can with Mountain View Peace and by shifting it further south.

02:26:59.960 --> 02:27:00.900
 That's there, Julie.

02:27:01.000 --> 02:27:02.700
 I think that's helpful to the conversation.

02:27:03.400 --> 02:27:06.580
 One of the problems is that we haven't been part of that conversation.

02:27:06.580 --> 02:27:17.860
 And so we're left to make assumption because we're looking at 162 acres that butts up against a neighborhood that's already greatly impacted by schools.

02:27:18.020 --> 02:27:22.220
 And frankly, had we had this conversation in front, we're probably not even having this conversation.

02:27:22.460 --> 02:27:28.740
 And just for perspective, I found out this location, I mean November meeting.

02:27:29.440 --> 02:27:38.300
 Months ago when we looked at the property and purchasing it, it was a very different location.

02:27:38.940 --> 02:27:45.100
 And I did try when we first had this on our agenda to reach out to Saratoga Springs where I represent.

02:27:45.100 --> 02:27:52.300
 And I do think that as we move forward, we have an issue of we have built a lot of schools in the wrong locations.

02:27:52.840 --> 02:28:06.880
 And we need to solve that going forward because all it creates is frustration and animosity between city officials, parents, students, staff, community.

02:28:07.140 --> 02:28:11.340
 And I think we can work to do that better.

02:28:12.340 --> 02:28:13.960
 I can't reach out on this one.

02:28:14.040 --> 02:28:16.900
 I will reach out even better on the next one.

02:28:17.060 --> 02:28:18.260
 I have a learning curve.

02:28:18.320 --> 02:28:22.080
 This is a question for both of you with the creation of new school district.

02:28:22.080 --> 02:28:30.340
 Does the board have the ability to create kind of their own guidelines, legislative processes, et cetera?

02:28:30.740 --> 02:28:36.740
 Or is that dictated by the state and you basically, it's just kind of a template that you adopt and away you go?

02:28:36.960 --> 02:28:44.500
 We create policies and we have flexibility and we could create a policy surrounding land purchase of a school.

02:28:44.920 --> 02:28:47.880
 I would be very interested in being part of that conversation.

02:28:48.260 --> 02:28:49.940
 Yeah, we could create a policy.

02:28:49.940 --> 02:29:00.480
 We could sit down and come up with something that would be very good about requiring the entities to work together for the best safe solution, not just land acquisition.

02:29:00.660 --> 02:29:12.600
 Right, because sometimes you guys buy the site that's cheaper, which I get, but it's not cheaper overall for the taxpayers because lights have to be put in, safe routes to school, and we've got to do that, right?

02:29:12.600 --> 02:29:17.880
 And so when we can lay all of that out and compare costs, I think it's helpful.

02:29:17.880 --> 02:29:24.600
 Again, when we created that policy or procedure, it would be binding on the district if there was disagreements.

02:29:24.940 --> 02:29:27.600
 I can't write policy or procedure that...

02:29:28.220 --> 02:29:48.660
 No, no, the reality is that that gives the Saratoga Springs City Council, Eagle Mountain City Council the opportunity to sit down and say, okay, let's put in our code some guiding principles for when developments are done that we're going to help identify by MBA or whatever, that this is a probable location, bring the school district in.

02:29:48.660 --> 02:29:49.660
 How do you feel?

02:29:49.660 --> 02:29:50.660
 How do you feel about this?

02:29:50.660 --> 02:30:03.100
 Things that we can do to mitigate the cost, because we understand that part of it, but also safe routes, putting into place that's the best service area for that area that will be a long-term service area, not, you know, that we tend to have at the very end.

02:30:03.100 --> 02:30:04.100
 Yeah.

02:30:04.100 --> 02:30:13.100
 I don't want to be in the position of prior priors where more skills just magically appear in cities.

02:30:13.100 --> 02:30:22.100
 I want to be a partner and I want to work because the infrastructure and the transportation in keeping students safe is key.

02:30:22.100 --> 02:30:32.100
 I'm wondering what state code, whether it's an MBA or something like that, if we can mandate to a developer this school site and their MBA?

02:30:32.100 --> 02:30:33.100
 I don't know if it can.

02:30:33.100 --> 02:30:35.100
 An MBA is a private contract.

02:30:35.100 --> 02:30:37.100
 You can put whatever you want in the MBA.

02:30:37.100 --> 02:30:50.100
 It's whatever both parties will agree.

02:30:50.100 --> 02:30:52.100
 We can't bind the school district to anything in an MBA.

02:30:52.100 --> 02:30:53.100
 No, no.

02:30:53.100 --> 02:30:54.100
 We're talking about a contractor.

02:30:54.100 --> 02:31:02.100
 Yeah, but if you're saying, oh, we're going to bind the developer to this is going to be a school site in the MBA, I mean, we have that.

02:31:02.100 --> 02:31:03.100
 That could happen.

02:31:03.100 --> 02:31:08.100
 In the harmony MBA, for example, we have like, these are school sites.

02:31:08.100 --> 02:31:09.100
 Guess what?

02:31:09.100 --> 02:31:10.100
 School district doesn't want them.

02:31:10.100 --> 02:31:12.100
 Again, I think that coordination.

02:31:12.100 --> 02:31:13.100
 That's kind of what, yeah.

02:31:13.100 --> 02:31:15.100
 So can we bind the contractor?

02:31:15.100 --> 02:31:16.100
 Sure.

02:31:16.100 --> 02:31:26.100
 But the Marcus's point, that may not be amenable to the school, but that's why we need to have them part of that conversation up front and say, does this meet your qualifications for topography?

02:31:26.100 --> 02:31:28.100
 We know that's an issue, right?

02:31:28.100 --> 02:31:31.100
 That's something that they can, they can weigh in on those things.

02:31:31.100 --> 02:31:37.100
 But yeah, I think having the conversations that we have not been having helps to have a better outcome.

02:31:37.100 --> 02:31:43.100
 We were meeting with the board and talking about those kinds of issues.

02:31:43.100 --> 02:31:53.100
 And then we got the school on the freeway and we, you know, so we were having those conversations and they said they wanted to be a part of it, but it just didn't.

02:31:53.100 --> 02:31:54.100
 I just don't feel like it's being communicated to the board.

02:31:54.100 --> 02:31:56.100
 I just don't feel like it's being communicated to the board.

02:31:56.100 --> 02:31:59.100
 They can create a policy that kind of gives the guidance.

02:31:59.100 --> 02:32:01.100
 Agreed, because then it's not a pinky problem.

02:32:01.100 --> 02:32:02.100
 That's right.

02:32:02.100 --> 02:32:11.100
 And again, trying to negotiate that and it's not a problem specific to your community or Saratoga Springs community.

02:32:11.100 --> 02:32:21.100
 I sat in a meeting with Lehigh community with frustration, so again, I think moving forward, my intent is to be a better partner.

02:32:21.100 --> 02:32:26.100
 I made baby steps in being a better partner with my city on this one.

02:32:26.100 --> 02:32:28.100
 Did I hit it out of the park?

02:32:28.100 --> 02:32:29.100
 Absolutely not.

02:32:29.100 --> 02:32:34.100
 Are there lots of steps to be taken and lots of procedures that could be done?

02:32:34.100 --> 02:32:42.100
 And I like the idea of looking at a procedure of this is what we do and this is how we work together.

02:32:42.100 --> 02:32:54.100
 So, JoLynn, even in a capital planning discussion, as this school site has shifted three times, it would be great to have that conversation with the city as you're shifting that, right?

02:32:54.100 --> 02:33:00.100
 Because this is the third site, first time I'm seeing it, and I've asked staff, have we seen any site at all? No.

02:33:00.100 --> 02:33:05.100
 Because knowing that's there, we probably would have alleviated this conversation.

02:33:05.100 --> 02:33:07.100
 If I wouldn't even have this conversation.

02:33:07.100 --> 02:33:15.100
 Right, but also the fact that we can see this property from Eagle Mountain without binoculars.

02:33:15.100 --> 02:33:17.100
 I didn't even throw a lock out of that.

02:33:17.100 --> 02:33:18.100
 I didn't throw a lock out of that.

02:33:18.100 --> 02:33:19.100
 I didn't throw a lock out of that.

02:33:19.100 --> 02:33:20.100
 I didn't throw a lock out of that.

02:33:20.100 --> 02:33:21.100
 I didn't throw a lock out of that.

02:33:21.100 --> 02:33:22.100
 100%.

02:33:22.100 --> 02:33:28.100
 So it's like you put a high school on our border and we talk to Saratoga, but we don't talk to Eagle Mountain.

02:33:28.100 --> 02:33:30.100
 Saratoga doesn't even feel like they got enough information.

02:33:30.100 --> 02:33:32.100
 So again, we just need to improve that.

02:33:32.100 --> 02:33:34.100
 Improving that, I think we can do.

02:33:34.100 --> 02:33:38.100
 Again, I just have very recently seen this shift.

02:33:38.100 --> 02:33:47.100
 A couple of things I do like about this is there are multiple roads that appear to be coming in from lots of different access points.

02:33:47.100 --> 02:33:51.100
 So we're not completely chokeholding one neighborhood.

