03:42:18.160 --> 03:42:19.160
 And --

03:42:19.160 --> 03:42:20.160
 Creating venues?

03:42:20.160 --> 03:42:21.160
 Yes.

03:42:21.160 --> 03:42:22.160
 Yeah, creating venues.

03:42:22.160 --> 03:42:33.160
 You know, like for example, do we put a little bit of money into Silver Lake or do we scrap that and do something totally different?

03:42:33.160 --> 03:42:34.160
 Yeah, bigger.

03:42:34.160 --> 03:42:35.160
 Go bigger.

03:42:35.160 --> 03:42:40.160
 But someone spending a little bit of time on that and coming back with a report.

03:42:40.160 --> 03:42:54.160
 Like, for example, yeah, no, Silver Lake is good for little stuff, but if you want -- if these are your goals, we need to go bigger, and this is what we can reach if we do go bigger, and this is going to be --

03:42:54.160 --> 03:43:02.160
 Maybe to your point, I mean, not to get to the end of the week with this, perhaps something that we already have, like a social camp theater.

03:43:02.160 --> 03:43:23.160
 We know that it's probably too small to be an effective concert series location, but maybe it's something that we could implement with the library for them to be able to view plays and small musicals and things like that, especially during the moment months, that would enable, you know, in working even with the --

03:43:23.160 --> 03:43:42.160
 with the Arts Alliance and other organizations as well that could be some of those smaller things, but we know that we want to have larger venues or where we can have concerts, where we can have pageants and things of that nature that maybe aren't going to all be inside, because we don't really have inside venues right now.

03:43:42.160 --> 03:43:43.160
 Yeah.

03:43:43.160 --> 03:43:44.160
 You've been to the American Fork Library.

03:43:44.160 --> 03:43:45.160
 Yes.

03:43:45.160 --> 03:43:47.160
 They have a little -- small theater.

03:43:47.160 --> 03:43:51.160
 It's not -- it's like for those kinds of things that you're talking about.

03:43:51.160 --> 03:44:12.160
 Eventually, we're going to need a much bigger theater, but for the little kids things and that kind of thing, but it's also great because if you have your legislators want to come in and talk and do an open house, there's room and it's comfortable instead of like a school setting where everybody's sitting on school chairs in a gym where they can't hear, you know, just --

03:44:12.160 --> 03:44:13.160
 It could be something that we can buy into the City Hall.

03:44:13.160 --> 03:44:18.160
 Well, I think that needs to be a part of the Library City Hall stuff.

03:44:18.160 --> 03:44:27.160
 People just preserve it, but they -- and they'll -- they'll preserve it for businesses as well, like businesses who want to have an employee meeting and don't have a place where they can all fit.

03:44:27.160 --> 03:44:31.160
 So, I agree with all the things that have been said.

03:44:31.160 --> 03:44:46.160
 To me, it's a priority to make sure that we feed into the things that are already trying to bring these things to us against many uphill battles and help facilitate those instead of creating things that compete with them.

03:44:46.160 --> 03:44:50.160
 So, we already have a community theater that does children's plays during the summer.

03:44:50.160 --> 03:44:55.160
 I think it'd be great if we could find a way to help them get connected better with the Library and --

03:44:55.160 --> 03:44:56.160
 That's kind of the way I'm looking at it.

03:44:56.160 --> 03:45:02.160
 It might be a way to make them more successful by allowing the Library to be a participant in that.

03:45:02.160 --> 03:45:08.160
 Well, and that's too -- when we talked about art funding, I said this is just visual right now.

03:45:08.160 --> 03:45:10.160
 We should be thinking about --

03:45:10.160 --> 03:45:13.160
