03:45:13.160 --> 03:45:15.160
 Perhaps they're -- they're separate.

03:45:15.160 --> 03:45:18.160
 And one is going to be -- this is the arts.

03:45:18.160 --> 03:45:24.160
 And this one is going to be basically art display kind of a thing.

03:45:24.160 --> 03:45:28.160
 So that we're -- that we can have specific focus on each of them.

03:45:28.160 --> 03:45:30.160
 And I don't think they're the same.

03:45:30.160 --> 03:45:35.160
 I think that we want to have two different focuses on those and funding sources.

03:45:35.160 --> 03:45:36.160
 Agreed.

03:45:36.160 --> 03:45:38.160
 I understand that they're different.

03:45:38.160 --> 03:45:42.160
 What I'm saying is I don't want us to forget about one of the branches of the arts.

03:45:42.160 --> 03:45:45.160
 In our effort to grow the other.

03:45:45.160 --> 03:45:46.160
 I don't think --

03:45:46.160 --> 03:45:48.160
 And I think that always needs to be a part of the conversation.

03:45:48.160 --> 03:45:50.160
 Yeah, but I think that they're very distinctly different.

03:45:50.160 --> 03:45:51.160
 I agree with that.

03:45:51.160 --> 03:45:54.160
 Because you've got a public art project.

03:45:54.160 --> 03:45:57.160
 Public art is -- it's visual by nature.

03:45:57.160 --> 03:45:59.160
 It just is.

03:45:59.160 --> 03:46:03.160
 And the community arts are no less valuable.

03:46:03.160 --> 03:46:04.160
 I'm not saying that they aren't.

03:46:04.160 --> 03:46:06.160
 It's just it's a different animal.

03:46:06.160 --> 03:46:11.160
 Because it's quite -- it's a little more nuanced.

03:46:11.160 --> 03:46:14.160
 And it's smaller, in my opinion.

03:46:14.160 --> 03:46:19.160
 And it's not something that every member of the community can participate in and take advantage of.

03:46:19.160 --> 03:46:23.160
 They could if they chose to, but they don't.

03:46:23.160 --> 03:46:26.160
 Public art is on display in the city hall setting.

03:46:26.160 --> 03:46:28.160
 It's for everyone's consumption.

03:46:28.160 --> 03:46:36.160
 You may hate it, but it's designed to compel an outcome for you to interact with it.

03:46:36.160 --> 03:46:40.160
 Either to engage with it and enjoy it and find satisfaction in it.

03:46:40.160 --> 03:46:43.160
 Or to literally dislike it, find displeasure in it.

03:46:43.160 --> 03:46:45.160
 And have a negative reaction from it.

03:46:45.160 --> 03:46:49.160
 So I -- it's just -- it's a different conversation, Melissa.

03:46:49.160 --> 03:46:50.160
 I agree.

03:46:50.160 --> 03:46:54.160
 The reason why I have to strengthen ends with others is I've lived in communities

03:46:54.160 --> 03:46:59.160
 where there was a hyper focus on one or the other.

03:46:59.160 --> 03:47:06.160
 And it didn't allow for the bazillion people in that community to develop and gravitate toward the things

03:47:06.160 --> 03:47:09.160
 that meet their needs and touch them.

03:47:09.160 --> 03:47:12.160
 I'm going to say, what I'm hearing, I don't think that's our problem here.

03:47:12.160 --> 03:47:15.160
 I think that we have people who are passionate on both sides of this.

03:47:15.160 --> 03:47:18.160
 And I think that we can support both of them equally.

03:47:18.160 --> 03:47:25.160
 I think you have the support on the council for the performing arts, the visual arts.

03:47:25.160 --> 03:47:30.160
 I think we've identified that there's support for doing some of those things that are representation

03:47:30.160 --> 03:47:32.160
 and character of who our city is.

03:47:32.160 --> 03:47:34.160
 I don't think it has to be one or the other.

03:47:34.160 --> 03:47:36.160
 One has to receive more focus than the other.

03:47:36.160 --> 03:47:40.160
 I think there are two different things that we can absolutely put equal focus on.

03:47:40.160 --> 03:47:41.160
 I agree.

03:47:41.160 --> 03:47:43.160
 Again, I don't like linear things.

03:47:43.160 --> 03:47:47.160
 I think we can attack things horizontally and all at the same time.

03:47:47.160 --> 03:47:49.160
 I just don't think you're hearing what I'm saying.

03:47:49.160 --> 03:47:51.160
 I don't disagree with you.

03:47:51.160 --> 03:47:56.160
 I just think that we need to have something in our process that makes sure that we look at both.

03:47:56.160 --> 03:47:58.160
 That's what I'm saying.

03:47:58.160 --> 03:48:00.160
 It could be different funding.

03:48:00.160 --> 03:48:02.160
 It could be a different process.

03:48:02.160 --> 03:48:03.160
 Are you feeling like we don't?

03:48:03.160 --> 03:48:04.160
 Is that what you're saying?

03:48:04.160 --> 03:48:05.160
 No.

03:48:05.160 --> 03:48:07.160
 I'm trying to understand what you're concerned about.

03:48:07.160 --> 03:48:09.160
 That's why I listed them separately.

03:48:09.160 --> 03:48:11.160
 So that they would both have a venue and art.

03:48:11.160 --> 03:48:13.160
 I'm trying to understand your concerns.

03:48:13.160 --> 03:48:18.160
 I'm asking questions because I don't understand what you're -- what are you concerned about?

03:48:18.160 --> 03:48:20.160
 Nobody's saying no to something.

03:48:20.160 --> 03:48:23.160
 I -- there must be a misunderstanding.

03:48:23.160 --> 03:48:24.160
 Just go ahead.

03:48:24.160 --> 03:48:25.160
 Good.

