 A Johnson's army reenactment would be awesome.

03:50:18.160 --> 03:50:19.160
 Freaking fantastic.

03:50:19.160 --> 03:50:20.160
 But also, you know --

03:50:20.160 --> 03:50:21.160
 That would be awesome.

03:50:21.160 --> 03:50:25.160
 We rode in a wagon this year for Pony Express Days.

03:50:25.160 --> 03:50:28.160
 And we can rent it every year for $1,500.

03:50:28.160 --> 03:50:31.160
 Or we can buy one for $3,000 or whatever, right?

03:50:31.160 --> 03:50:35.160
 And at some point, my goal is to have a bunch of wagons.

03:50:35.160 --> 03:50:38.160
 The reality is it shouldn't just be on Pony Express Days.

03:50:38.160 --> 03:50:42.160
 We have -- do you remember the wagon we used to do during Christmas?

03:50:42.160 --> 03:50:43.160
 Yeah.

03:50:43.160 --> 03:50:45.160
 Everybody comes down and -- it didn't cost them a thing.

03:50:45.160 --> 03:50:49.160
 The volunteers -- I mean, all of Jared's people were coming with their horses,

03:50:49.160 --> 03:50:54.160
 hooking up to wagons, and taking people on this simple little ride just around the park.

03:50:54.160 --> 03:50:57.160
 And they were lined up like 50, 60 people deep.

03:50:57.160 --> 03:51:00.160
 That's the kind of traditions that are meaningful.

03:51:00.160 --> 03:51:05.160
 Within our community, think a little bit bigger with the tourism aspect.

03:51:05.160 --> 03:51:09.160
 When people will come for the Olympics the year preceding and the year after,

03:51:09.160 --> 03:51:12.160
 they will be like, "Fun things to do in Utah."

03:51:12.160 --> 03:51:17.160
 If we have a stagecoach ride or something that takes them on --

