 I don't anticipate that my list is comprehensive.

03:52:34.160 --> 03:52:35.160
 There's probably a few things.

03:52:35.160 --> 03:52:38.160
 You can find if we just focus on a handful and start.

03:52:38.160 --> 03:52:39.160
 Yeah.

03:52:39.160 --> 03:52:40.160
 Just kind of start.

03:52:40.160 --> 03:52:43.160
 It's going to branch out to there.

03:52:43.160 --> 03:52:44.160
 One other one.

03:52:44.160 --> 03:52:46.160
 Sorry to interrupt you.

03:52:46.160 --> 03:52:51.160
 One other one that I think is crucial, and this more is IT.

03:52:51.160 --> 03:53:15.160
 In the IT world of all of the IT managers for cities and directors, they have, what's it called, a mutual aid agreement that some of them have gotten into so that when there's a catastrophic attack or something like that, all the bright minds from the other cities can come together and help you because it's more than you can get down by yourself.

03:53:15.160 --> 03:53:22.160
 I know Provo for sure has been working on something like that because their IT director was talking to me about it.

03:53:22.160 --> 03:53:42.160
 But there's also a crap ton of really bright people in our community where not only could we look at security for us in the city, but maybe we could up our offerings from a STEM perspective and those really bright minds could come and present at the library or something like that.

03:53:42.160 --> 03:53:45.160
 So IT I think is an important community we should start there.

03:53:45.160 --> 03:53:46.160
 Yeah.

03:53:46.160 --> 03:53:47.160
 Yeah.

03:53:47.160 --> 03:53:48.160
 That's valid.

03:53:48.160 --> 03:53:59.160
 On my list I only have one more item and that is agriculture as an industry, as a business.

03:53:59.160 --> 03:54:16.160
 So if, the reason I put it that way is because if we're going to, it's more than even just keep agriculture here because even our agriculture is not where it needs to be.

03:54:16.160 --> 03:54:17.160
 Yeah.

03:54:17.160 --> 03:54:33.160
 And in an ever changing world, we're going to need to find what does agriculture of the future look like and how can we ensure that it has life here and help expedite that and help clear the way.

03:54:33.160 --> 03:54:43.160
 Because even, you know, even the cattle industry, you know, don't grazing that, you know, the natural tendency of that is it just gets pushed out, which, okay.

03:54:43.160 --> 03:54:49.160
 I mean, we might decide we can live with that or we might decide we want something different.

03:54:49.160 --> 03:54:58.160
 And, but a committee could look at that and decide what, what's reachable, what can be done and what we want to do.

03:54:58.160 --> 03:55:07.160
 Because frankly, as I have talked to state people and no one's doing it, it's just not happening.

03:55:07.160 --> 03:55:09.160
 So this is another thing.

03:55:09.160 --> 03:55:12.160
 We're impacting the cultural uses in Utah.

03:55:12.160 --> 03:55:14.160
 We're pushing our food sources out.

03:55:14.160 --> 03:55:15.160
 We are.

03:55:15.160 --> 03:55:18.160
 And frankly, we're kind of doing it as a country right now.

03:55:18.160 --> 03:55:23.160
 It's going to get to the point where we're importing beef from Brazil and Argentina.

03:55:23.160 --> 03:55:24.160
 Yep.

03:55:24.160 --> 03:55:25.160
 Yep.

03:55:25.160 --> 03:55:27.160
 And, you know, I mean, there's always going to be a certain amount of that.

03:55:27.160 --> 03:55:29.160
 But what is our comfort level?

03:55:29.160 --> 03:55:30.160
 Where do we want to land?

03:55:30.160 --> 03:55:31.160
 Where do we want to be in the long run?

03:55:31.160 --> 03:55:36.160
 Well, I think the job can teach people some self-sufficiency of how we can use this land.

03:55:36.160 --> 03:55:41.160
 And even the things that we've seen over at the school for the big building.

03:55:41.160 --> 03:55:48.160
 That's my hope is that will be the seed, you know, propelling into the future.

03:55:48.160 --> 03:55:50.160
 But, yeah, what does this look like?

03:55:50.160 --> 03:55:56.160
 I mean, I wanted to reach beyond just simple home gardens kind of a thing or even community gardens.

03:55:56.160 --> 03:56:02.160
 I want to, like, can we, can we sustain elements of agriculture?

03:56:02.160 --> 03:56:03.160
 With a limited water.

03:56:03.160 --> 03:56:04.160
 Like a city?

03:56:04.160 --> 03:56:05.160
 Yeah.

03:56:05.160 --> 03:56:06.160
 Under our circumstances.

03:56:06.160 --> 03:56:10.160
 With our lousy soils and limited water in short seasons.

03:56:10.160 --> 03:56:11.160
 What can we do?

03:56:11.160 --> 03:56:12.160
 Yeah.

03:56:12.160 --> 03:56:16.160
 I just feel like you would take a committee to invest that time.

03:56:16.160 --> 03:56:18.160
 I think there are things that can be done.

03:56:18.160 --> 03:56:19.160
 We won't be able to do everything.

03:56:19.160 --> 03:56:22.160
 You know, we're not going to grow, probably not going to grow bananas here.

03:56:22.160 --> 03:56:23.160
 Right?

03:56:23.160 --> 03:56:24.160
 But cattle, definitely.

03:56:24.160 --> 03:56:28.160
 So we want to make sure that we're clearing the way for cattle.

03:56:28.160 --> 03:56:29.160
 Is, you know.

03:56:29.160 --> 03:56:31.160
 Corn and wheat can be grown here.

