03:58:00.160 --> 03:58:06.160
 But as you're saying this, I'm kind of thinking perhaps this is a replacement for citizen boards.

03:58:06.160 --> 03:58:10.160
 So I don't know that how, whether I'm one way or the other on that.

03:58:10.160 --> 03:58:11.160
 Yeah.

03:58:11.160 --> 03:58:12.160
 All right.

03:58:12.160 --> 03:58:13.160
 So here's what I had.

03:58:13.160 --> 03:58:15.160
 Economic Development Committee.

03:58:15.160 --> 03:58:27.160
 I think that enables us to bring in some of our biggest and brightest in the city and help to have some of those connections that maybe we're trying to foster, but they already exist.

03:58:27.160 --> 03:58:28.160
 That's something that could be helpful.

03:58:28.160 --> 03:58:30.160
 Roads and Engineering Committee.

03:58:30.160 --> 03:58:36.160
 Parks, Open Space, and Cemetery Committee that would address some of the things that you've talked about.

03:58:36.160 --> 03:58:46.160
 Planning, Building, and DRC Committee that maybe could, you know, Brandon's been talking about an architectural review board type thing.

03:58:46.160 --> 03:58:55.160
 In fact, it absolutely exists within that that helps us specific, especially if we're talking about like a downtown architectural review.

03:58:55.160 --> 03:59:04.160
 It can exist within that or even some of the things that we're talking about that we're wanting to do overlays with that we want to utilize for specific economic benefit.

03:59:04.160 --> 03:59:12.160
 Um, and then Neighborhood Improvement and Historical Preservation Committee, not the neighborhood improvement that we talk about now.

03:59:12.160 --> 03:59:17.160
 I'm talking about actual revitalization and caring for the neighborhoods.

03:59:17.160 --> 03:59:18.160
 And beautification.

03:59:18.160 --> 03:59:21.160
 Beautification and historical preservation could have that.

03:59:21.160 --> 03:59:28.160
 Because it wouldn't be, historical preservation, it would not be busy necessarily every single month about that, perhaps.

03:59:28.160 --> 03:59:31.160
 But that could be one of the things that could accomplish.

03:59:31.160 --> 03:59:36.160
 Uh, the more I think about this one, I think there's, this is probably a necessary thing.

03:59:36.160 --> 03:59:38.160
 A water, storm, water, and sewer committee.

03:59:38.160 --> 03:59:44.160
 Where they deal with what our assets are, what our needs are going to be with each of these things,

03:59:44.160 --> 03:59:52.160
 and help us, you know, kind of become our warning of, we're approaching dangerous levels of whatever.

03:59:52.160 --> 03:59:53.160
 They could also do something.

03:59:53.160 --> 03:59:54.160
 Or usage is too high, et cetera.

03:59:54.160 --> 03:59:57.160
 Like some community classes.

03:59:57.160 --> 04:00:02.160
 In a lot of ways, how Central Utah Water has different things like that.

04:00:02.160 --> 04:00:08.160
 That might be something that there's a community education aspect that they can tie in with the library.

04:00:08.160 --> 04:00:14.160
 And maybe even come up with some incentives to get people to participate by a training program or something like that.

04:00:14.160 --> 04:00:16.160
 Uh, a lot of things that could be done with that.

04:00:16.160 --> 04:00:18.160
 Uh, a lot of things that could be done with that.

04:00:18.160 --> 04:00:20.160
 Public Safety, Military, and Veterans Committee.

04:00:20.160 --> 04:00:21.160
 Be able to address those.

04:00:21.160 --> 04:00:26.160
 Because again, I don't know that each of those needs something every single meeting.

04:00:26.160 --> 04:00:31.160
 But perhaps that's a way for the public to be involved in, you know, coming to you and saying,

04:00:31.160 --> 04:00:34.160
 "Look, we have a real problem at this park that keeps getting graffiti.

04:00:34.160 --> 04:00:35.160
 How are we going to address this?

04:00:35.160 --> 04:00:36.160
 What are some of the solutions?"

04:00:36.160 --> 04:00:37.160
 Et cetera.

04:00:37.160 --> 04:00:41.160
 Uh, also community relations, events, and recreation.

04:00:41.160 --> 04:00:45.160
 Because I feel like the three of those kind of go hand in hand.

04:00:45.160 --> 04:00:52.160
 Uh, how we're, our events and our recreation are one of the ways that we kind of present ourselves

04:00:52.160 --> 04:00:53.160
 to the community, right?

04:00:53.160 --> 04:00:57.160
 And to have the community relations and how we're getting that information out.

04:00:57.160 --> 04:01:02.160
 I think that helps us to kind of stay on the tip of the sword.

04:01:02.160 --> 04:01:06.160
 Uh, Library, Public Education, and Election Committee.

04:01:06.160 --> 04:01:10.160
 Uh, I, I remember we talked about this a little bit.

04:01:10.160 --> 04:01:13.160
 I remember we added the Elections Committee on there to maybe take some of the burden off

04:01:13.160 --> 04:01:18.160
 with staff for that to allow them to engage with the county.

04:01:18.160 --> 04:01:20.160
 Uh, but I don't know exactly how that works.

04:01:20.160 --> 04:01:23.160
 I just remember writing that down for a couple of years.

04:01:23.160 --> 04:01:26.160
 Would it be one that also leads out, like, with the debates and things like that?

04:01:26.160 --> 04:01:27.160
 That's what we were thinking.

04:01:27.160 --> 04:01:28.160
 And meet the candidates?

04:01:28.160 --> 04:01:31.160
 Yeah, that they would kind of take that off the hands of them

04:01:31.160 --> 04:01:36.160
 and set up maybe multiple debates and also come up with, they would spend the time putting

04:01:36.160 --> 04:01:41.160
 together candidate information and the distribution of that, et cetera.

04:01:41.160 --> 04:01:47.160
 So that then the election official could have focused on the election, but this is more of like a-

04:01:47.160 --> 04:01:50.160
 Yeah, so I mean it really can be a lot of things, right?

04:01:50.160 --> 04:01:52.160
 But that would help maybe take some of the burden off it.

04:01:52.160 --> 04:01:55.160
 Then the last one, so I had a Legislative and Code Committee.

04:01:55.160 --> 04:01:57.160
 I don't know where I'm at on that one anymore.

04:01:57.160 --> 04:02:00.160
 I don't remember why I put that one on there.

04:02:00.160 --> 04:02:07.160
 But I did add the two that you added, the Mayor, the Power Committee and the Agriculture as a Business Committee.

04:02:07.160 --> 04:02:09.160
 I think that there's some benefit to that.

04:02:09.160 --> 04:02:16.160
 And honestly, I hope we have farmers that are on that and even cattlemen that are doing those types of things.

04:02:16.160 --> 04:02:24.160
 But man, it would be awesome if we could get somebody from an act school to be a Board Mayor on that, to help us.

