04:02:46.160 --> 04:02:49.160
 Can I offer some comments?

04:02:49.160 --> 04:02:53.160
 Pro Bowl had a really robust committee system.

04:02:53.160 --> 04:02:59.160
 But it wasn't a third the length of this list.

04:02:59.160 --> 04:03:13.160
 One of the concerns that I would have is the ability of a committee to meet and generate more work for the staff, especially if you've got staff participating in these meetings.

04:03:13.160 --> 04:03:15.160
 Be aware of that.

04:03:15.160 --> 04:03:18.160
 I think that's one of the important parts of that.

04:03:18.160 --> 04:03:19.160
 Yeah.

04:03:19.160 --> 04:03:22.160
 We should absolutely utilize virtual with this.

04:03:22.160 --> 04:03:24.160
 They don't need to be sitting in the same room.

04:03:24.160 --> 04:03:25.160
 Oh, that's not what I'm going with.

04:03:25.160 --> 04:03:30.160
 What I'm going with it is just the ability to create work and staff time involved in all those things.

04:03:30.160 --> 04:03:33.160
 We had kind of a policy around it.

04:03:33.160 --> 04:03:35.160
 And what we had was very similar.

04:03:35.160 --> 04:03:39.160
 We had one less than what it took to make it an open public meeting.

04:03:39.160 --> 04:03:42.160
 We had staff assigned.

04:03:42.160 --> 04:03:51.160
 One of the things our council members really found helpful was that somebody take notes for the meetings and then share them with the rest of the council so they at least know what's going on.

04:03:51.160 --> 04:03:58.160
 And then you don't take as much time up in, say, a public meeting unless you have something you specifically want to talk about.

04:03:58.160 --> 04:03:59.160
 I really like that.

04:03:59.160 --> 04:04:00.160
 That's…

04:04:00.160 --> 04:04:03.160
 But my caution is just be aware of the two things.

04:04:03.160 --> 04:04:12.160
 The workload on staff to be part of all these and the amount of extra workload you can create out of ideas that come out of those committees.

04:04:12.160 --> 04:04:14.160
 But that said, I'm a fan of committees.

04:04:14.160 --> 04:04:17.160
 I find them to be very effective and helpful.

04:04:17.160 --> 04:04:20.160
 Just be aware of how many and how often those kinds of things.

04:04:20.160 --> 04:04:21.160
 Yeah.

04:04:21.160 --> 04:04:35.160
 In fact, I'm not sure if this is what you're saying or not, but one of the things I thought of is there may be advantages to keeping them sort of ad hoc level because then they don't have to jump through all the hoops that an official organization would.

04:04:35.160 --> 04:04:36.160
 Right.

04:04:36.160 --> 04:04:43.160
 It's really just from my perspective, I see the committee as just an idea generation of the factory.

04:04:43.160 --> 04:04:44.160
 Yeah.

04:04:44.160 --> 04:04:45.160
 That's what I see it as.

04:04:45.160 --> 04:04:48.160
 Which is great, but those ideas become work.

04:04:48.160 --> 04:04:49.160
 And that's what I'm saying.

04:04:49.160 --> 04:04:56.160
 Like, I love the committee structures, but my office had five employees, plus we were bringing in somebody from…

04:04:56.160 --> 04:05:01.160
 I guess the way I see that converting into work is that it's going to get through a council priority.

04:05:01.160 --> 04:05:02.160
 Yeah.

04:05:02.160 --> 04:05:03.160
 To be able to…

04:05:03.160 --> 04:05:04.160
 Yeah.

04:05:04.160 --> 04:05:05.160
 Yeah.

04:05:05.160 --> 04:05:06.160
 That's how I see it.

04:05:06.160 --> 04:05:07.160
 Yeah.

04:05:07.160 --> 04:05:11.160
 But I think Cliff is also referring to even just time commitments to staff.

04:05:11.160 --> 04:05:14.160
 So I think that's very important for us to report that.

04:05:14.160 --> 04:05:15.160
 Yeah.

04:05:15.160 --> 04:05:21.160
 And I think we need to maybe evaluate what Rich was saying because if we're going to do these committees…

04:05:21.160 --> 04:05:28.160
 To probably replace the board, we may want to look at replacing the boards because I think

04:05:28.160 --> 04:05:34.160
 that's a lot to ask of staff to be… have to sit on boards and all of these committees…

04:05:34.160 --> 04:05:36.160
